    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "BLUF",
      "narration_text": "The short version, before any detail. The whole toolkit reads fourteen environment variables and runs on one contract. And the gate that broke last week was never really broken. I was running it from the wrong place.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type-on",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "BrutalistHesitantWriter",
          "props": {
            "face": "serif",
            "align": "center",
            "fontSize": 200,
            "lineSpacing": 1.16,
            "charMs": 18,
            "hesitateBetween": 0,
            "hesitateWithin": 0,
            "mistakeRate": 0,
            "jitter": 5,
            "text": "Not a few variables.\nFourteen of them.\nAnd the gate I broke\nwas never broken."
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-26T17:34:06.511769+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 16,
      "actual_duration_s": 11.86,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 11.875,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:BrutalistHesitantWriter",
        "at": "2026-10-26T15:04:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "WHAT",
      "narration_text": "So how does the system work. You write a beat sheet. The toolkit generates the narration locally, and that audio becomes the clock. Every beat is then rendered to the length of its own mp3. Then the gates run. Then you get a master. Nothing downstream can change the timing, because the timing was decided by the voice.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeTldrWhat",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "PROGRESS",
            "heading": "Audio first, then everything else",
            "question": "So how does the pipeline actually run?",
            "folderLabel": "@HumanitariansAI",
            "lines": [
              "Narration is generated first",
              "Its length becomes the clock",
              "Every beat is cut to fit"
            ],
            "greeting": "",
            "topic": ""
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B02.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-26T19:01:17.316617+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 22,
      "actual_duration_s": 16.51,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 16.541666666666668,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeTldrWhat",
        "at": "2026-10-26T15:04:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "TERMS",
      "narration_text": "Two variables do most of the work, and you never set either one. ART underscore HOME is the toolkit root. The art script works it out from where the script itself lives, then exports it. REEL underscore DIR is your reel folder, turned into an absolute path before anything runs.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeDefinitions",
          "props": {
            "title": "Two you never set",
            "folderLabel": "@HumanitariansAI",
            "terms": [
              {
                "term": "ART_HOME",
                "meaning": "The toolkit root. art finds it itself"
              },
              {
                "term": "REEL_DIR",
                "meaning": "Your reel, made an absolute path"
              }
            ]
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B03.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-26T17:29:03.107412+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 20,
      "actual_duration_s": 15.36,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 15.375,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeDefinitions",
        "at": "2026-10-26T15:04:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "EVIDENCE",
      "narration_text": "And here are the ones you can set. The Kokoro model and voice files. A Remotion timeout that defaults to one hundred and eighty thousand milliseconds. A switch that turns off drawn text. And which ffmpeg to use. Every one of them has a default. None of them is magic.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeCodeBeat",
          "props": {
            "title": "env.sh",
            "language": "bash",
            "largeText": true,
            "brandLabel": "Irreducibly Human",
            "sparkLine": "Defaults, not magic.",
            "code": "export KOKORO_MODEL=kokoro-v1.0.onnx\nexport KOKORO_VOICES=voices-v1.0.bin\nexport ART_REMOTION_TIMEOUT_MS=180000\nexport ART_NO_DRAWTEXT=1\nexport FFMPEG=ffmpeg"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B04.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-26T17:40:12.678013+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 20,
      "actual_duration_s": 14.53,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 14.541666666666666,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeCodeBeat",
        "at": "2026-10-26T15:04:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "FINDING",
      "narration_text": "And here is the part that explains last week. I had already installed the missing library. The gate still would not run. The blocker was never the library. It was the interpreter. Line nine ninety nine of the checker uses a type annotation that needs python three point ten. The system python here is three point nine point six. The toolkit ships its own environment at three point thirteen, and inside that one everything runs.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeCodeBeat",
          "props": {
            "title": "check.sh",
            "language": "bash",
            "largeText": true,
            "brandLabel": "Irreducibly Human",
            "sparkLine": "Not the library. The interpreter.",
            "code": "python3 -c \"import scipy\"\n# ok — 3.9.6 has it\npython3 type_check.py $REEL\n# TypeError: float | None\nsource .venv/bin/activate\n# 3.13.12 — runs"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B05.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-26T18:01:25.783338+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 22,
      "actual_duration_s": 21.27,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 21.291666666666668,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeCodeBeat",
        "at": "2026-10-26T15:04:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "act": "JUDGE",
      "narration_text": "So what do I take from week two. A tool that depends on its environment will fail in ways that look like bugs. Reading the setup first would have saved me a week of suspicion. And every default in that list is a decision somebody already made for me. Knowing which ones I can move is the actual skill.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeTldrWhy",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "PROGRESS",
            "heading": "The lesson from week two",
            "lead": "The tool was fine. My shell was not.",
            "folderLabel": "@HumanitariansAI",
            "lines": [
              "Read the setup before blaming it",
              "A default is someone else's choice",
              "Know which ones you can move"
            ],
            "greeting": "",
            "topic": ""
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B06.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-26T19:02:12.246964+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 21,
      "actual_duration_s": 15.77,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 15.791666666666666,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B06.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeTldrWhy",
        "at": "2026-10-26T15:04:33"
      }
    },
